    <h2>Classic DQ Cake vs. Blizzard Cake — What's the Difference?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Classic DQ Cake</strong> — Standard vanilla and chocolate soft serve with fudge and crunch layers. The original DQ celebration cake. Available in 8-inch and 10-inch.</li>
      <li><strong>Blizzard Cake</strong> — Uses a specific Blizzard flavor (Oreo, Cookie Dough, Reese's, or Choco Brownie Extreme) blended into the soft serve layer. The actual mix-in pieces (cookie pieces, candy, brownie) are distributed throughout the cake. Costs more than the classic version.</li>
      <li><strong>Sheet Cake</strong> — Rectangular format for large events. Feeds 24–32 people. Available in classic DQ flavor.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How to Order a DQ Cake — Step by Step</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Step 1</strong> — Call or visit your local DQ at least 48 hours before the event. Some locations allow online ordering via the DQ app.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 2</strong> — Choose your size: 8-inch (8–10 people), 10-inch (12–16 people), or Sheet Cake (24–32 people).</li>
      <li><strong>Step 3</strong> — Choose your flavor: Classic DQ, Oreo Blizzard, Cookie Dough Blizzard, Reese's Blizzard, or Choco Brownie Extreme.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 4</strong> — Add your personalized message and choose colors. Some locations accept photo toppers.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 5</strong> — Pick up at least 30 minutes early to allow time if adjustments are needed.</li>
    </ul>
